WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:04.033
-Also, we are so excited
on this holiday week,

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:07.734
the final shows of 2023,
to have our dear friend

00:00:07.734 --> 00:00:10.334
and bandleader Fred Armisen
back with us on drums.

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:14.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thanks.

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:16.133
-Fred, once again,

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:18.267
no one has accomplished more
in 2023 than you.

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:20.300
You're always working. We're
happy when we have you here.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.868
We also know that you're out
on the road doing stand up,

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:25.801
doing other projects,
and I'm always just blown away

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.467
when I hear the things
you're working on.

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:28.567
-Aww, thank you.

00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:30.467
-And I have to ask you,
is this true

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:34.234
that you are releasing this week
your own Christmas album?

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.868
-I am.
-Wow.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you. Yeah.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:39.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:42.601
It's a celebration
of the Mummy.

00:00:42.601 --> 00:00:44.367
You know, like...

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:46.934
-The -- The horror movie
character of the Mummy?

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:49.167
-Yeah. Well, people think of it
as a horror movie character,

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:51.734
but it's just a character
for all seasons.

00:00:51.734 --> 00:00:54.000
So I'm just trying
to do something

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.801
so, like, to include the Mummy

00:00:55.801 --> 00:00:58.501
in more Christmassy,
you know, things.

00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:01.033
And it's just like, you know --
-When you say, like, "more,"

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:02.534
like, I would say,
like, start --

00:01:02.534 --> 00:01:05.033
we're starting at zero, right?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.033 --> 00:01:07.334
Like, I feel like there are
zero holiday classics

00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:09.200
that include
the Mummy right now.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.300
-You're right about that...
-Yeah.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.601
-...actually.

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:13.901
And this is just a way
to bring that back.

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:15.734
Because Christmas --
-But, again, you say "back"...

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:17.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:19.601
Was there a time when there were
a lot of Mummy Christmas songs?

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:21.667
-Just the old traditions,
you know what I mean?

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:23.567
Like the old -- Like,
let's bring that back,

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:25.767
like the 1800s
and, you know, like...

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:28.267
-So in the 1800s, there were
a lot of Christmas songs

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:29.934
that had the Mummy in them?
-I gather.

00:01:29.934 --> 00:01:32.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:35.133
-Did you do any research?
-Some. I --

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:36.467
You know,
the way I do research

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:37.667
is I've got a bunch of friends.

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:39.234
They are awesome.
I think they're here.

00:01:39.234 --> 00:01:41.334
You guys are great.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.267
You guys are here.

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:45.200
-So it sounds -- It sounds like
maybe the whole audience.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.367
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:48.567
-It's most of them,
and they're the best.

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:50.000
They're like --
But they're the best.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.534
They're -- They work so hard.
They're just so cool.

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:54.400
They're down to earth,
they're sweet.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.701
And they --
-I know you've been really

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:57.100
keeping it under wraps, but...

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.567
And you don't have to have
any music for it.

00:01:58.567 --> 00:02:00.834
Just, you know, a cappella,
could you just real quick

00:02:00.834 --> 00:02:02.434
sing us one of your Mummy
Christmas songs?

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:04.234
-Oh, well, first of all,
it's just melodies.

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:05.467
They're Mummy melodies.

00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:07.467
So there's no --
it's not the lyrics.

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:10.400
It's just like...
[ Vocalizing ]

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:14.701
-So, I'm sorry.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.100
You're telling me --
I've seen the cover art.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:20.601
It's you with your arm around
a Mummy wearing a Santa hat.

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:22.467
-Yes.
-So I buy that...

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:25.501
there's an expectation I'm going
to hear Mummy holiday songs,

00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:27.033
and it's all just melodies?

00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:28.734
-But you're going to picture
the mummies

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:30.634
walking around at Christmas.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:32.567
That's what you're
supposed to imagine.

00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:35.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:36.834
-How many songs are on it?

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:38.100
-22.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:40.968
-Give it up for Fred Armisen,
everybody!

